<BaseLayout title="How we review software" description="Read SelectVerdict's transparent methodology for sourcing facts, assessing software, verifying information, and handling affiliate relationships."><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'How we review' }]} /><PageIntro eyebrow="Editorial methodology" title="How we turn sources into useful decisions." description="Our process separates verifiable product facts from editorial analysis and makes uncertainty visible." /><article class="section narrow prose"><h2>1. Define the decision</h2><p>We begin with the buyer, use case, and constraints. This prevents a long feature list from standing in for practical guidance.</p><h2>2. Gather primary evidence</h2><p>We prioritize official documentation, pricing pages, security materials, terms, and direct product information. Credible independent sources may add context. Each material fact should connect to a reference and an access date.</p><h2>3. Verify and classify claims</h2><p>Content records distinguish <strong>verified facts</strong>, <strong>editorial assessments</strong>, and <strong>unverified research notes</strong>. Unverified notes are not presented as established facts. Published product records include a last-verified date.</p><h2>4. Assess fit and tradeoffs</h2><p>Our verdict structure identifies who a product may suit, who it may not suit, notable strengths, and meaningful limitations. These are editorial judgments, labeled as such and explained by an evidence basis.</p><h2>5. Review before publication</h2><p>We check internal consistency, links, disclosure status, and whether the conclusion is supported. We do not assign fake ratings or imply hands-on use. If direct testing occurs, the page should explicitly describe its scope and method.</p><h2>6. Maintain and correct</h2><p>Software changes. Verification dates communicate freshness, and material corrections should be made when reliable new evidence appears.</p><h2>Affiliate relationships</h2><p>Commercial relationships are recorded per product and disclosed on relevant pages. Compensation does not determine inclusion, ranking, or conclusions. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p></article></BaseLayout>
